{
  "$comment": "INPUTS ONLY. Every machine oracle has been removed for blind development: `expected` on each vector and `content_hash` on each pack. The prose `why` fields are kept \u2014 they are documentation a foreign implementer would legitimately read. The full frozen file, oracles included, is revealed only after this implementation has emitted its own results.",
  "acceptance_criterion": "Two independent implementations receiving the same packs, in any input order, must either produce the same effective manifest by value identity and the same canonical hash, or produce the same typed refusal.",
  "canonicalization": {
    "adr": "ADR-0002",
    "canonical_json": "json.dumps(data, sort_keys=True, separators=(',',':'), ensure_ascii=True, allow_nan=False).encode('utf-8')",
    "hash": "'v1:' + sha256(canonical_json(data)).hexdigest()",
    "note": "Reused verbatim from dsm_primitives. No new hashing law is introduced. An implementation that reproduces these hashes with its own canonicalizer has proven the canonicalizer too."
  },
  "governs": "ADR-PACK-0001 \u2014 Pack Composition, Precedence and Resolution Refusal",
  "how_to_use": [
    "For each vector, assemble its pack documents from `packs` (a SET \u2014 the listed order is transport only).",
    "Call resolve(packs, evaluated_at, resolver_version) and compare against `expected`.",
    "Resolved: the effective manifest must match by VALUE IDENTITY and its canonical hash must equal effective_manifest_hash.",
    "Refused: the phase, the COMPLETE refusal set and refusal_hash must all match. 'It failed' is not a pass.",
    "Re-run every vector under every permutation of its input order. Any permutation-dependent output is a defect, not a variation.",
    "A vector whose pack carries schema_valid=false must still be run: the resolver refuses it on its own, without relying on schema validation having happened."
  ],
